    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0703" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v28/pg671"/>

                <head>345. Note From the President’s Special Assistant (Rostow) to President
                        Johnson<anchor n="1" xml:id="d345-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1968-03-19T12:20:00-05:00">March 19, 1968, 12:20 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. President:</p>
                <p>You may wish to take into account at lunch<anchor n="2" xml:id="d345-f2"/> these
                    thoughts of the meeting of the Southeast Asian Ambassadors and Gen. Westmoreland
                    at Cam Ranh Bay.</p>
                <p>They raise, among other matters, the possibility of: <list>
                        <item>—a feint against North Vietnam;</item>
                        <item>—limited operations in Laos.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold"> W.W. Rostow </hi>
                    </signed><anchor n="3" xml:id="d345-f3"/>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d345-a1.xml" xpointer="d345-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d345-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d345-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Country File, Vietnam, Cambodia
                    5 E (2)a, 1/68–10/68. Top Secret.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d345-f2" n="2" xml:id="d345-f2-content">
                <p>According to the notes of the March 19 Tuesday luncheon meeting, neither this
                    cable nor the issues that it raised were discussed. (Ibid., Tom Johnson’s Notes
                    of Meetings, 3/19/68)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d345-f3" n="3" xml:id="d345-f3-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this typed signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
